{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.j2" as M %}
{% block content %}
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      {{ M.eyebrow("CRM upgrade") }}
      <h1>From enquiry sheet <em>to a real CRM.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">When more than one person handles enquiries, a Google Sheet starts to slip. We move your factory's enquiries, customers and follow-ups into Zoho Bigin in about a week. Your website and IndiaMART leads then flow straight in.</p>
      <div class="row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Talk to us about a CRM</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/services/">See all packages</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="answer"><b>In short:</b> setup costs <b>from ₹20,000, one time</b>, and is ready in about a week. You pay for the software directly to Zoho, in your company's name. Bigin is free for one user. Paid plans start at <b>₹400 per user a month</b> on yearly billing, before GST.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup> We run Sutrayaan's own enquiries on Bigin the same way.</p>

        <h2>Three steps, at your pace</h2>
      </article>
      <div class="path3">
        <div><span class="step">Step 1</span><h3>Website</h3><p>A site that shows what you make, with a quote form that accepts drawings.</p></div>
        <div><span class="step">Step 2 · free at launch</span><h3>Enquiry tracker</h3><p>Every enquiry saved to a Google Sheet, with an instant email alert. Enough for one or two people.</p></div>
        <div class="now"><span class="step">Step 3</span><h3>CRM upgrade</h3><p>Zoho Bigin for the whole sales team: deals, follow-up tasks, WhatsApp and reports.</p></div>
      </div>
      <article class="prose">

        <h2>Signs you have outgrown the sheet</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Two or more people reply to enquiries, and nobody is sure who answered whom.</li>
          <li>Quotes go out, but follow-ups depend on someone remembering.</li>
          <li>Enquiries arrive from the website, IndiaMART, WhatsApp and phone calls, in different places.</li>
          <li>You can't quickly answer "how many quotes did we send last month, and how many did we win?"</li>
          <li>A salesperson leaves, and their customer history leaves with their phone.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we set up</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
          <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>What it means for you</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><b>Bigin account in your name</b></td><td>The account, data and licence belong to your company, on Zoho's India data centre.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Your sales stages</b></td><td>A pipeline that matches how you sell, e.g. Enquiry, Drawing received, Quote sent, Sample, Won or Lost.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Website enquiries as deals</b></td><td>Each quote request becomes a company, contact and deal, with a "reply within 24 hours" task for the right person.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Your history imported</b></td><td>Past enquiries and customers from your sheet or Excel, so nothing starts from zero.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>IndiaMART and TradeIndia leads</b></td><td>Connected so new leads land in Bigin automatically, through the marketplace's lead feed or a connector tool, where your plan allows.<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>WhatsApp</b></td><td>Chat with buyers from inside Bigin, on Express plans and above.<sup><a href="#s3">3</a></sup></td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Training and support</b></td><td>One hour with your team on phone and laptop, then 30 days of help.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>

        <h2>What it costs</h2>
        <p>Our setup fee is one-time. The Zoho licence is a separate yearly bill from Zoho. Prices below are Zoho's India list prices on yearly billing, before GST.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
          <thead><tr><th>Team size</th><th>Setup (Sutrayaan)</th><th>Bigin Express licence (Zoho)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1 user</td><td>From ₹20,000</td><td>Free plan, or ₹4,800 a year on Express</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3 users</td><td>From ₹20,000</td><td>₹14,400 a year</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5 users</td><td>From ₹25,000</td><td>₹24,000 a year</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>
        <p>Zoho also offers Premier (₹720 per user a month) and Bigin 360 (₹1,080) for larger teams.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup> The free plan suits a single owner. It has one pipeline, 500 records and few automations, so for a team we suggest Express.<sup><a href="#s4">4</a></sup></p>

        <h2>Why Zoho Bigin</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Simple.</b> It is Zoho's CRM for small teams. It is built around a pipeline you drag deals through, not dozens of menus.</li>
          <li><b>Affordable.</b> Paid plans start at about half the price of Zoho's full CRM.<sup><a href="#s4">4</a></sup></li>
          <li><b>Room to grow.</b> If you outgrow it, Zoho supports moving up to Zoho CRM later.<sup><a href="#s4">4</a></sup></li>
          <li><b>Indian.</b> Zoho is an Indian company with data centres in India.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We are independent. You always pay Zoho's own list price, directly to Zoho. If we ever earn a referral fee from Zoho for your sign-up, we will tell you up front. It never changes your price.</p>

        <h2 id="growing">For growing manufacturers and exporters</h2>
        <p>Bigin suits teams of up to about ten people with a simple sales process. Larger firms usually need more: export quotes, dealer networks, approvals and reports across teams. Often the software is not the real problem. The process is.</p>
        <p>For these firms we work in two steps.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>What happens</th><th>Cost and time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><b>1. Process review</b></td><td>We map how an enquiry becomes a quote, an order, a dispatch and an invoice. We talk to sales, production and accounts, mark where things slip, and recommend what to fix and which Zoho apps fit.</td><td>From ₹15,000 · 1–2 weeks. Credited if you go ahead with step 2.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>2. Zoho CRM setup</b></td><td>Pipelines for direct buyers, dealers and export markets. Quotes and price lists with approvals. Website, IndiaMART and email enquiries in one place. An owner dashboard, team training and 60 days of support.</td><td>From ₹75,000 · 4–8 weeks</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>
        <p>The Zoho CRM licence is paid to Zoho, from about ₹800 per user a month on yearly billing, before GST.<sup><a href="#s4">4</a></sup> If you also need accounts, inventory or HR in the same system, we tell you during the review. Where needed, we bring in a certified Zoho partner for that part.</p>

        <div class="faq" style="margin-top:12px">
          <details><summary>Do I need a website from you to get the CRM upgrade?</summary><p>No. We can set up Bigin on its own and connect your existing website form, IndiaMART and WhatsApp. It works best with a quote form we control, because each enquiry then arrives with full details.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Who owns the data in the CRM?</summary><p>You do. The Bigin account is in your company's name and you pay Zoho directly. You can export your data any time.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Will my team actually use it?</summary><p>That is why we keep it small: a few stages, a follow-up task for each enquiry, and the phone app. Training is done on the phones your team already uses.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can it send quotes and invoices?</summary><p>Bigin tracks deals and follow-ups. For quotes and invoices, Zoho has separate apps that connect to it. We can advise when you need them.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Do you work with larger manufacturers and exporters?</summary><p>Yes. For larger teams we start with a paid process review, then set up Zoho CRM around how you actually sell. Setup starts at ₹75,000, and the review fee is credited if you go ahead.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What if I already use Excel or another CRM?</summary><p>We import your existing customers and enquiries into Bigin as part of the setup.</p></details>
        </div>

        <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
        <ol class="sources">
          <li id="s1"><a href="https://www.bigin.com/articles/bigin-india-pricing-clarification.html" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Bigin: official India pricing</a></li>
          <li id="s2"><a href="https://www.pabbly.com/how-to-add-indiamart-leads-to-zoho-bigin-as-contacts-using-pabbly-connect/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Pabbly: adding IndiaMART leads to Zoho Bigin</a></li>
          <li id="s3"><a href="https://help.zoho.com/portal/en/kb/bigin/faqs/trouble-shooting-faqs/articles/whatsapp-integration-in-bigin-messages" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Zoho Help: WhatsApp integration in Bigin</a></li>
          <li id="s4"><a href="https://codroiditlabs.com/?p=10211" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Bigin vs Zoho CRM: plans and limits (checked November 2026)</a></li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

{{ M.cta_band("Ready to stop losing <em>follow-ups?</em>", "Tell us how your team handles enquiries today. We'll reply within 24 hours with a fixed quote for the move to Bigin.") }}
{% endblock %}
